{number: 164}
{title: Come, Holy Spirit}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Come, Holy Spirit, [F] heav'nly [C] Dove,
With all Thy quick'ning [G7] pow'rs;
[C] Kindle a flame of [F] sacred [C] love
In these cold [G7] hearts of [C] ours.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Look [C] how we grovel [F] here be-[C] low,
Fond of these earthly [G7] toys;
Our [C] souls, how heavily [F] they [C] go
To reach e-[G7] ternal [C] joys.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In [C] vain we tune our [F] formal [C] songs,
In vain we strive to [G7] rise;
Ho-[C] sannas languish [F] on our [C] tongues,
And our de-[G7] votion [C] dies.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Dear [C] Lord, and shall we [F] ever [C] live
At this poor dying [G7] rate?
Our [C] love so faint, so [F] cold to [C] Thee,
And Thine to [G7] us so [C] great!
{end_of_verse}
